  "question": {
    "text": "A line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> intersects the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math> at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the midpoint of the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>coordinate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> then which one of the following options is correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0005_6dc3d599a5b0.png\"/>\r\n\r\nEquation of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\nLet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be the mid point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>, so its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-coordinate of midpoint <math><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>\r\n\r\nHence, coordinates of midpoint <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>\r\n\r\nLet centre of circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>\r\n\r\nSince, perpendicular dropped from centre upon any chord divides it in two equal parts.\r\n\r\nHence, line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> will be perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>O</mi></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo><</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
